From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: fan53555: cache the registers

Every voltage change is a read-modify-write of the VSEL register through
an uncached regmap. That register also holds the buck enable bit, so a
read that comes back corrupted turns the next DVFS step into a write that
switches the CPU rail off. On the PineTab 2 (TCS4525 on the i2c bus it
shares with the PMIC) the tablet resets - a silent power-on reset - within
a few frequency changes under heavy NEON load, and it stops doing so as
soon as no voltage writes happen at all; the size of the step does not
matter, one 6.25 mV step resets it just the same.

Cache the registers: the DVFS hot path becomes a single write, and a
transfer that goes wrong can no longer feed back into the enable bit.
The monitor register stays volatile.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN rc_a/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c rc_b/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c	2026-09-19 07:30:14.463101636 +0200
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c	2026-09-19 07:44:43.602869319 +0200
@@ -627,9 +627,26 @@
 	return PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(rdev);
 }
 
+static bool fan53555_volatile_reg(struct device *dev, unsigned int reg)
+{
+	/* The monitor register reports live status; everything else is ours. */
+	return reg == FAN53555_MONITOR;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Cache the registers. Every voltage change is a read-modify-write of the
+ * VSEL register, which also carries the buck enable bit, so a read that
+ * comes back wrong turns the next DVFS step into a power-off of the CPU
+ * rail. With a cache the hot path is write-only, and it is one transfer
+ * instead of two on a bus shared with the PMIC.
+ */
 static const struct regmap_config fan53555_regmap_config = {
 	.reg_bits = 8,
 	.val_bits = 8,
+	.max_register = TCS4525_COMMAND,
+	.volatile_reg = fan53555_volatile_reg,
+	/* a tree cache: a register never read comes from the hardware once */
+	.cache_type = REGCACHE_MAPLE,
 };
 
 static struct fan53555_platform_data *fan53555_parse_dt(struct device *dev,
